[Result "0-1"]
[WhiteElo "2763"]
[BlackElo "2785"]
[ECO "C81"]
[Opening "Ruy Lopez: Open, Howell Attack"]

{Ruy Lopez: Open, Howell Attack. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 ! Be6 {Here the exchange is tempting and wrong: trading the good bishop leaves the dark squares bare.} (8... Nd2 Nbxd2 b4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Qe2 Be7 10. Rd1 O-O 11. c4 bxc4 ?! 12. Bxc4 f5 13. Nc3 Nxc3 14. bxc3 Qd7 15. Bf4 Na5 16. Bd3 c5 17. Rab1 h6 18. Bxa6 Qa4 19. Be3 Rab8 20. Bb5 Qg4 21. h3 Qh5 22. a4 f4 23. Bd2 Qg6 24. Bd3 Bf5 25. Bxf5 Qxf5 26. Rb5 Nc4 27. Bc1 Qe4 28. Qa2 Kh8 29. Re1 Qd3 30. Bd2 Ra8 31. Rb7 Rfe8 32. Qb1 Qxb1 33. Rexb1 Rxa4 34. Rd7 Bg5 35. Be1 Nxe5 36. Rxd5 Nxf3+ 37. gxf3 Rc4 38. Kg2 Bf6 39. Rb7 Kh7 40. Bd2 Re2 41. Rd3 Kg6 42. Rbd7 Bg5 43. Kf1 Re6 44. R7d5 Rf6 45. Rd6 Ra4 46. Rxf6+ Bxf6 47. Kg2 Rc4 48. Rd5 Bxc3 49. h4 Bf6 50. Bxf4 Kf7 51. Bd2 Be7 52. Rd3 Rd4 53. f4 Rxd3 54. Be3 Rd5 55. Kf3 g6 56. Ke4 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} Rf5 0-1

